---
<article class="border-l-4 border-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] pl-6">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">October 12, 2026</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
    Added vehicle mileage tracking to the finance copy. A breeder logs business trips per vehicle with a
    destination and purpose, links each trip to the animals, buyers, and breeding plans it was for, and
    sees the IRS standard-rate deduction in the Tax Figures on the Tax Year P&amp;L. The copy does not
    claim GPS tracking, tax advice, or that the deduction reduces profit.
  </p>

  <div class="mb-4">
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Pages updated</h3>
    <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
      <li><a href="/workflows/invoicing-expenses" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/workflows/invoicing-expenses</a>: new mileage section, two FAQ entries (with matching FAQPage structured data), and a line in the page summary.</li>
      <li><a href="/for-breeders" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/for-breeders</a>: a mileage bullet in Business &amp; Finances.</li>
      <li><a href="/features" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/features</a>: a Vehicle Mileage Tracking card in Finance &amp; Contracts (from <code>src/lib/planFeatures.ts</code>).</li>
      <li><code>llms.txt</code> and the OKF product bundle now list vehicle mileage logs under business tools.</li>
    </ul>
